<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Document xmlns:p="property" xmlns:r="reflection" Id="Q8S0C99eUM2ILSyP3Tjw4a" LanguageVersion="2025.7.4" Version="0.128">
  <NugetDependency Id="SIMDywDLwNbQ5UdOPHQxYD" Location="VL.CoreLib" Version="2025.7.4" />
  <NugetDependency Id="Sm17wEPgUJCVB75op3gzPF" Location="VL.Skia" Version="2025.7.4" />
  <NugetDependency Id="CCoTJSCcdlnfZwmjUnPFVB" Location="VL.Mapsui" Version="0.0.0" />
  <!--
    NetTopologySuite is declared HERE, by this document, and that is not the same as VL.Mapsui
    declaring it. VL.Mapsui's own declaration is what lets its node signatures name NTS types; a
    patch that wants to use NTS nodes itself needs its own dependency on it. Measured: without this
    line the node below is "Not found"; with it, it resolves.
  -->
  <NugetDependency Id="KkbVvAgR3UtmSGnGV4pAoR" Location="NetTopologySuite" Version="2.6.0" />
  <!--
    VL.NetTopologySuite is the package that MAKES geometry; this one draws it. VL.Mapsui's nuspec
    depends on it so that opening this patch does not greet you with red nodes - vvvv does not
    fetch a missing document dependency by itself, it shows it red and offers to install on
    rightclick.
  -->
  <NugetDependency Id="QVnZMbPyNO4lv6YFocyiqT" Location="VL.NetTopologySuite" Version="0.0.0" />
  <NugetDependency Id="UJ4lOiV4ddMRDp3IepvNro" Location="VL.GeoJSON" Version="0.0.0" />
  <Patch Id="FJzZkKqVfW12i9kQk6L0hz">
    <Canvas Id="N0E8bKG5vqG1aLaGsfcogC" DefaultCategory="Main" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <!--

    ************************ Application ************************

-->
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,100" Id="Pt4eKK7Ag0dikcitT4Vmar">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <FullNameCategoryReference ID="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="T1yChjTcVpcQLJ4rxMEL44">
        <Canvas Id="VxYLn5bECvkjhyGerEE3sc" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="VaZNqihOnpwz6dORWEdpu0" Bounds="-1560,-40,860,1180" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="A mountain.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Fuji, from the top. Nine coordinates typed in by hand, and the trails read from a file.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE NINE ARE THE PEAKS ROUND THE CRATER - 剣ヶ峰 3776, 白山岳 3756, 伊豆岳 3749, 成就岳 and 三島岳&#xD;&#xA;3734, 朝日岳 3733, 久須志岳 3725, 浅間岳 3722, 駒ヶ岳 3718. Walking all of them is お鉢巡り, going&#xD;&#xA;round the bowl. They are listed in WALKING order, not by height: reorder them by height and the&#xD;&#xA;ring tangles across the crater instead of round it. Order is part of the geometry, not a detail of&#xD;&#xA;presentation.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;SAME NINE NUMBERS, THREE THINGS:&#xD;&#xA;  a walk        -&gt; LineString   the rim path, open&#xD;&#xA;  the rim       -&gt; LinearRing -&gt; Polygon   closed, so it has an inside&#xD;&#xA;  the summit    -&gt; Point        the first one alone. The highest ground in Japan.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Not a trick - it is what that place IS. Somewhere you walk, an edge round a hole, and a spot you&#xD;&#xA;stand on. Which one you mean is a thing you declare, and here you declare all three at once.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;SWITCH ON &quot;SHOW THE TRAILS&quot; for the four routes up: 吉田, 富士宮, 須走, 御殿場, plus 河口湖 - 41&#xD;&#xA;segments out of OpenStreetMap, with the huts and the other peaks. Your typed ring should sit&#xD;&#xA;exactly on their crater.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE HUTS ARE A LADDER, not a scatter, and their heights are in the file: 御来光山荘 2795,&#xD;&#xA;日ノ出館 3040, 赤岩八合館 3290, 見晴館 3400, 万年雪山荘 3410, 胸突山荘 3550, 頂上富士館 3740.&#xD;&#xA;LabelStyle can print any of that - point its Attribute at &quot;name&quot; or &quot;ele&quot;.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;COLOUR THEM BY THEIR HEIGHT - you can, now. When this prompt was written that was a wall: no&#xD;&#xA;node chose a style from an attribute VALUE, and the gap sat first on this family&apos;s list. Then&#xD;&#xA;StyleByValue closed it (2026-08-23). Point its Attribute at &apos;ele&apos;, Min 2700, Max 3776, between a&#xD;&#xA;pale style and a deep one, and the huts climb in colour as they climb the mountain. Prompt Live&#xD;&#xA;earthquakes and Prompt Paint by numbers are built on exactly that node - this mountain was the&#xD;&#xA;second thing the gap stopped, and the reason it was worth closing.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;TRY IT WITH YOUR OWN MOUNTAIN. Nine coordinates is an evening&apos;s work and every mountain has a&#xD;&#xA;shape somebody would recognise. Peaks are in OpenStreetMap as natural=peak, usually with ele.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Attribution is on the map because it has to be: the trails are OpenStreetMap, ODbL, and the credit&#xD;&#xA;belongs wherever the data is SHOWN.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="UnaIkq8cPr0a4UZQVn7ji7" Comment="Enabled" Bounds="79,280,35,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="false">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="ImmutableTypeFlag" Name="Boolean" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:buttonmode p:Assembly="VL.UI.Forms" p:Type="VL.HDE.PatchEditor.Editors.ButtonModeEnum">Toggle</p:buttonmode>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="CNYLiTg3BUtmCJlFwHyUjv" Comment="Cache To Disk" Bounds="207,280,35,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="true">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="ImmutableTypeFlag" Name="Boolean" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:buttonmode p:Assembly="VL.UI.Forms" p:Type="VL.HDE.PatchEditor.Editors.ButtonModeEnum">Toggle</p:buttonmode>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Node Bounds="79,340,150,19" Id="JqwwJBWIvaSJq4DTAz8vuN">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Mapsui.Layers" LastDependency="VL.Mapsui.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
