          </Node>

          <!--
            ***** one style per geometry type *****

            A SymbolStyle draws POINTS AND NOTHING ELSE. Not a fainter polygon - none of it, zero
            pixels, no error anywhere. Measured: a polygon covers 14884 px under a VectorStyle,
            956 under NO STYLE AT ALL, and 0 under a SymbolStyle. Mapsui picks a renderer by the
            style's runtime type, and it does not help that SymbolStyle derives from VectorStyle.

            So a layer holding more than one kind of geometry needs StyleByGeometry, which hands
            each feature the style for ITS OWN kind. Every mapping library works this way:
            OpenLayers takes a style function returning styles[geometry.getType()], Mapbox GL
            splits circle / line / fill into separate layer types, Leaflet has pointToLayer beside
            style, a QGIS layer is single-geometry-type with its own renderer.

            DO NOT stack instead. Sending a VectorStyle and a SymbolStyle to one layer together
            does draw the polygon - and puts a SECOND circle on every point, because a VectorStyle
            draws its own 32 pixel marker there too. Measured: Scale 0.6 is 22 px across alone and
            34 px stacked, which is simply the default. Dispatch, do not stack.
          -->
          <Pad Id="EsoJaRP1I65f0rJfLdwzWW" Comment="Shape" Bounds="520,420,110,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Ellipse">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Mapsui.Styles" LastDependency="VL.Mapsui.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="SymbolShape" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="E2tJMBZkwB64ZplxWXqbUf" Comment="Scale - 1 is 32 pixels" Bounds="520,445,150,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="0.8">
